.TH LINUX-HELLO-CLI 1 "October 2026" "Linux Hello" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linux-hello-cli \- manage face authentication
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linux-hello-cli
[\fB\-U\fR \fIUSER\fR] [\fB\-y\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIargument\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Front end for the Linux Hello service. Model, target and setting commands
need no root; polkit asks for a password where needed. Commands marked
(root) open the camera or edit files directly.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Service state and whether your face is enrolled.
.TP
.B doctor
Check camera, data files, models and PAM targets.
.TP
.BR list ", " add " [\fIlabel\fR], " remove " \fIid\fR, " rename " \fIid label\fR, " clear
Manage the face models of the user.
.TP
.B targets
Show where face unlock can be used.
.TP
.BR enable ", " disable " \fItarget\fR"
Use face unlock for \fBlock-screen\fR, \fBadmin\fR (polkit), \fBsudo\fR or \fBlogin\fR, or stop.
.TP
.B set \fR[\fB\-\-section\fR \fIsection\fR] \fIoption value\fR
Change a setting. Local settings live in /etc/linux-hello/config.ini, the
documented defaults in /usr/share/linux-hello/config.ini.
.TP
.B cameras
List usable cameras, best first.
.TP
.BR test ", " snapshot " (root)"
Live camera preview, or save a snapshot.
.TP
.B config \fR(root)
Edit the local settings file.
.TP
.B reset-system \fR[\fB\-\-purge\fR] (root)
Undo every PAM change made by Linux Hello. With \fB\-\-purge\fR also delete
face models, settings and logs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-U\fR, \fB\-\-user\fR \fIUSER\fR
Act on another user's models (needs admin).
.TP
.B \-y
Skip confirmations.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine readable output.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/360900/linux-hello
